      "spam": false,
      "value": "Private rooms are essentially what you're looking for and they're already in the game.\n\nYes most players are on desktop, would it really be a good idea to push these people away from the game? Desktop players are of course going to responsible for most bad behavior but that doesn't mean VR players aren't either just because they paid for the $700 DLC.\n\nAlso players that want to intentionally hack/disrupt the game will always exist no matter what, IF they are able to, this is a weird thing to suggest. Hackers are not dealt with by exiling half the community, this is a separate problem that is resolved by restricting people from doing said bad things.\n\nFor me what would detract from the experience? If 1/3 of the players was playing PC only, 1/3 VR only and 1/3 both.\n\nA lot of desktop players are great and of course you want to bring them to your private VR rooms. How do you think you became friends with these people?\n\nThe main target group shouldn't be VR users it should be everyone, VR is a place that should be seen as a place where people can go to be something else, whatever they want to be, with VRchat desktop players can have this too. Also the more people that buy a VR the better, the more money pumped into VR the faster it'll progress, (hopefully) I can't speak for everyone's intentions, sometimes more money can be made by slowing down.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
