      "value": "@{5a608a476e91f9643e46b709|full_name}: This is more about  behavior/social interaction than the hacking.\n\nPrivate rooms do not allow for meeting random people and the majority of unchill players on desktop.\n\nDesktop players wouldnt be pushed out of the game and VR players would still choose to hang out in open-to-all public rooms at any time they wanted to.\n\nFor the Desktop players that _cant_ make friends with VR users very little would change, the small percentage of users on VR they meet would just get a little smaller.\n\nDesktop users that are cool and can befriend VR users would also enjoy this feature since it would also get them away from the free-to-play-lets-troll-everyone desktop users.\n\nI know id go into \"gen pop\" to hang out when i was in the mood for the random of open-to-all public rooms but sometimes that isnt the case and i find myself longing back to before the desktop explosion when desktop users were a minority and it was a lot more chill.\n\nThe desktop user base could stay the same since the game is still playable like today except that those who can make friends would benefit.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
