      "value": "@{58c6b3cc227a56787575ebb4|full_name}: Nobody who's angry or hates can think logically about something. It's not possible, all I can see from your posts here is that you really dislike the fact that there's people that can play using desktop but the truth is there's a lot of great people playing on desktop and the game would be a different place without them. The only point I want to make is the way you're feeling and thinking negatively about this will not give you the right answer and it will in fact make your experience when you play worse if you keep a mindset like this. With this VR/desktop issue it's very complicated, even if everyone who came to this post spent hours trying to design a perfect system for this we wouldn't reach the best answer, just because there's so many factors at play, this is something that I'm sure the VRchat team is thinking about, but it's something that really need careful planning over a period of time by people that really know what they're doing.\n\nSo I can understand how you feel but stressing over this isn't the right way to go, I can say for sure something will come to improve the situation regarding trolls etc. But the answer will be a compromise, between desktop and VR and it's something that doesn't have a right answer, it's more about finding a good balance between the too, with slightly more emphasis on the side of VR. In the future as more people are starting to use VR then they can start to let go of the desktop side a little bit. But right now, especially for the growth of VRchat AND VR both sides need to be respected.\n\nAt the end of the day I'm sure that we can all agree that any player who wants to have fun on VRchat desktop user or VR is welcome. The main concern is with the trolls and anyone who maybe doesn't take the game quite as seriously. And it's clear that VRchat is thinking about this, if someone is disruptive or breaking game rules then they aren't welcomed on the game no matter what they're using. So at the end of the day the best way to make this situation better is by focusing on methods of dealing with \"toxic\" players first, as that's the root cause of this problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
