  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-17T20:01:25.414Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I know there are private rooms but hear me out:\n\nThe overwhelming majority of players are on desktop, i dont think im wrong when i state that they are responsible for the overwhelming majority of bad behavior and likely disruptive hacking.\n\nThis can really detract from the experience for everyone.\n\nA setting when creating an instance that makes it visible to VR users only seems like a reasonable thing to me.\n\nA lot of desktop users are great though, those desktop users that are friends with VR users could be invited to the VR rooms, basically a way of \"vetting\" the desktop users that get in.\n\nI know i would still go out into \"gen pop\", the randomness can be very fun when one is in the mood, but not always.\n\nThis wouldnt solve all the issues VRchat is currently facing but make it better for the main target group, the VR users.",
